--- a driver that cannot read a profile is refused, by name
CREATE-FILE: connection 'plaindir' names driver dir, which does not read connection profiles -- it would take "@plaindir" for a location of its own.  Bind to dir directly instead.
--- and nothing is left behind named for the reference
0
--- an undefined profile says so
CREATE-FILE: connection 'nosuch' is not defined (SET-CONNECTION nosuch driver=... address=...)
--- and one that exists but names no driver says THAT
CREATE-FILE: connection 'nodriver' does not say which driver it uses (SET-CONNECTION nodriver driver=...)
--- sqlite puts the database where the profile says
